  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given methyl phenyl ether can be prepared from&nbsp;Williamson Ether Synthesis.&nbsp;Williamson Ether Synthesis usually takes place as an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math> reaction of a Alkyl halide with an alkoxide ion. Aryl halides cannot be used in this reaction. The reaction is given below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cabe1b84-ce1a-42a8-8133-d132c3aebf8d.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 83px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
